# terraria (translated client): world creation from the menu. First run with an EMPTY save root (NO_WORLD=1):
# language -> title -> Single Player -> New player -> the player list -> the (empty) world list -> New ->
# UIWorldCreation: Small, Classic, evil Random, typed name "ref_small", typed seed "12345" -> Create ->
# the loading screen (UIWorldLoad) while WorldGen.worldGenCallback runs on a worker fiber -> the world list ->
# enter the world. UI elements are found by their own snap points (aim snap NAME [ID]), not by pixel.
# Run: NO_WORLD=1 sh crates/terraria-app/scripts/run_hidden.sh crates/terraria-app/scripts/g15_create_world.input g15_create_world 3600
# (the first lines are g5_world_select.input)
# (character creation) -> Create with a typed name -> the player list -> select the player -> world select.
# Ticks are shell ticks (fixed 1/60 s step). See g1_title.input for the first 1200 ticks.
frame 900 mouse 640 360
# "English" is the first entry of the language list (first run only: no config.json yet)
frame 1010 mouse 640 247
frame 1030 click left
frame 1100 mouse 900 600
frame 1200 shot ../work/shots/g1_title.png
# hover "Single Player" (highlight + tick sound), then click it
frame 1210 mouse 640 250
frame 1240 shot ../work/shots/g1b_title_hover.png
frame 1250 click left
frame 1330 mouse 900 650
frame 1400 shot ../work/shots/g2_player_select.png
# "New" on the player select screen
frame 1410 mouse 807 650
frame 1430 click left
frame 1500 mouse 1100 680
frame 1560 shot ../work/shots/g3_character_creation.png
# "Create": the name prompt opens; type a name and confirm
frame 1570 mouse 770 533
frame 1590 click left
frame 1650 shot ../work/shots/g3b_name_prompt.png
frame 1660 text Porter
# Enter arrives as a typed character (WM_CHAR 13): Main.GetInputText reads it from the IME key listener
frame 1700 text \n
frame 1800 mouse 1100 680
frame 1860 shot ../work/shots/g3c_player_list.png
# the play button of the player's row: world select
frame 1870 mouse 348 311
frame 1890 click left
frame 1960 mouse 1100 680
frame 2020 shot ../work/shots/g4_world_select.png
# the world list is empty: "New" opens UIWorldCreation
# (UIWorldSelect's "New" and "Back" panels have no snap point: "New" is at the place of the player list's "New")
frame 2030 dump ui
frame 2030 mouse 807 650
frame 2050 click left
frame 2110 mouse 1100 690
frame 2120 dump ui
frame 2125 shot ../work/shots/g15a_world_creation_default.png
# size Small (id 0 of Small / Medium / Large)
frame 2130 aim snap size 0
frame 2150 click left
# difficulty Classic (the buttons are Journey, Classic, Expert, Master: id 1)
frame 2170 aim snap difficulty 1
frame 2190 click left
# evil Random (id 0 of Random / Corruption / Crimson): the default, clicked anyway
frame 2210 aim snap evil 0
frame 2230 click left
# the name plate: the virtual keyboard page, typed text, Enter
frame 2250 aim snap Name
frame 2270 click left
frame 2330 text ref_small
frame 2370 text \n
# the seed plate
frame 2440 aim snap Seed
frame 2460 click left
frame 2520 text 12345
frame 2560 text \n
frame 2630 mouse 1100 690
frame 2650 dump ui
frame 2655 shot ../work/shots/g15b_world_creation_filled.png
# screenshots while the generation is suspended at its yield points (the script's clock stands still then)
frame 2660 loadshots ../work/shots/g15c_generating_{}.png 150 40
frame 2670 aim snap Create
frame 2690 click left
# --- generation runs here ---
frame 2760 mouse 1100 690
frame 2800 dump ui
frame 2800 dump world
frame 2805 shot ../work/shots/g15d_world_list_after.png
# the play button of the new world's row
frame 2810 aim snap Play 0
frame 2830 click left
frame 2900 mouse 900 500
frame 3170 dump world
frame 3170 dump player
frame 3170 dump npcs
frame 3180 shot ../work/shots/g15e_ingame.png
# Save & Exit is not needed for the file comparison: the world file is written by WorldFile.SaveNewWorld
frame 3240 quit
